{"qid":"Q215","names":["Republic of Slovenia"],"title":"Republic of Slovenia","endonym":{"native":"Slovenija","lang":"sl"},"capsule":"Slovenia declared independence from Yugoslavia on 25 June 1991 following a referendum in which 88 percent voted to secede, and gained international recognition — first by Germany and Austria — on 15 January 1992. A brief Ten-Day War (27 June–7 July 1991) against Yugoslav federal forces ended with the Brioni Agreement; the Yugoslav People's Army withdrew, making Slovenia's departure essentially bloodless relative to other Yugoslav successor conflicts. Slovenia joined NATO in March 2004 and the European Union on 1 May 2004, adopting the euro on 1 January 2007, and hosted the EU Council presidency in 2008 and 2021.","attestation":"Boundaries from Seshat Cliopatria (Bennett et al., Scientific Data 2025; CC BY 4.0), digitized from standard historical atlases at ~0.07° resolution. Borders are fully internationally recognized and precisely delimited, with the exception of a longstanding maritime boundary dispute with Croatia in the Gulf of Piran, which was adjudicated by an international tribunal in 2017 but remains contested in practice.","attestationLinks":[{"label":"Cliopatria dataset (Seshat, CC BY 4.0)","url":"https://github.com/Seshat-Global-History-Databank/cliopatria"},{"label":"Bennett et al. 2025, Scientific Data","url":"https://www.nature.com/articles/s41597-025-04516-9"}],"citations":[{"label":"Wikipedia: Slovenia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovenia"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Slovenian independence referendum, 1990","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slovenian_independence_referendum,_1990"},{"label":"Wikipedia: Ten-Day War","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ten-Day_War"}],"britannica":"place/Slovenia","cowCode":null,"wikipedia":"Slovenia","rulers":[{"qid":"Q282653","name":"Lojze Peterle","start":1990,"end":1992,"image":"Lojze Peterle 2024.jpg","imageUrl":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/Special:FilePath/Lojze%20Pe